current_round.prompt:
Recover the retained one-click source-upgrade implementation from current main while preserving all four failed rounds, branches, reflogs, logs, worktrees, and candidates 0272a2f5e320bfad995e5fe8c7a1402dd06aa45c, ebf9a1e0bf22b3082bf71a70082b1c595ff1093f, 8c86eb10abc27391e8a1f7fa0fa5700818f029d8, and 5311e885fa0abd01f9998d3089af37304a221726. Reuse or replay the Round 4 candidate as a baseline; do not relax Governance Rule 4 or replace the bounded restart-safe helper with unsupervised bespoke behavior.

Close the remaining launch-boundary crash window with a two-phase, operation-correlated handoff protocol. Persist a reservation/preparing state that is explicitly not proof of helper liveness; submit exactly one helper carrying the operation id plus a unique attempt/claim token; durably record a launch receipt or atomic helper claim; only then transition to an active restart_safe_handoff stage. Startup recovery must decide from correlated receipt, claim, and live process/helper evidence—not stage text alone:
- reservation before successful submission becomes visibly interrupted and retryable;
- submission before receipt must reconcile the exact helper, atomically adopt one verifiably live claimant or terminate/settle ambiguity, never assume liveness;
- a received/claimed live helper may be adopted across daemon restart;
- late helpers after interruption and duplicate helpers/retries must be rejected by durable attempt ownership;
- zero, duplicate, stale, or ambiguous claimants must produce visible recoverable failure evidence rather than a permanently running operation;
- cancellation, rollback, workflow-admission restoration, post-restart verification, and operation/process projections must remain correlated to the same authoritative attempt.

Keep reservation, receipt/claim, activation, interruption, and retry transitions in the shared source-promotion/operation capabilities with idempotent replay. Add deterministic crash-point tests for before submission, after submission/before receipt, after receipt/before activation, helper claim/adoption after restart, late-helper rejection, duplicate retry suppression, cancellation races, and registration/rollback restoration. Exercise the real launcher boundary and systemd handoff where supported; distinguish platform-gated evidence. Rerun focused source-promotion, operation-recovery, daemon lifecycle, provider, CLI/web/static tests, generated CLI reference, full Rust tests, strict Clippy, cargo check/fmt, and git diff --check. Read back any workflow completion signal written by the agent. Do not approve, merge, rewrite history, delete retained evidence, or directly edit durable Goal state.

